/-!
# KIL3: the network of one Prop. 11 level on one stack (bits)

The `W` wire streams (bits, `ZMod 2`, encoded as the integers `0, 1`) are kept on stack `0` as a
table (`KIL3Tab`).  A gate `g` with touched set `S`:

1. for every `w ∈ S` (in order), the frame change `Φ (M_g − lab w)` is run in place on stream `w`
   (`applyC`, the stream code is any stack-`0` program, e.g. with child calls);
2. the table is rebuilt: a touched stream becomes the sum mod 2 of the touched streams with
   coefficient `1` in row `w` of the gate matrix, an untouched stream is copied.

At the end the final frame changes `Φ (Mout w − lab w)` are run on every stream.
`netC_runs`: the code computes `netRunF` (`AModelProp11`) with `Φ` given by the stream codes,
cost `Σ_frames (cE + 2·cOp) + Σ_gates (cRebuild + 2) + 1` (`O(V)` per frame and per gate,
`W` and the gate list fixed).
